    "segments": [
      {
        "role": "david",
        "speaker": "David",
        "sourceStart": 7,
        "sourceEnd": 190,
        "text": "Thanks for coming to this extra community garden meeting. We have 500 pounds left for this year. We've already spent most of the grant on tools and seeds, so this is our final budget.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "58a3c57ef6e0a876d59b8994267e4ff9eae96633bcc47706488727d286aa9b7a",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0
      },
      {
        "role": "anna",
        "speaker": "Anna",
        "sourceStart": 197,
        "sourceEnd": 316,
        "text": "The council says we can't use the money for anything that isn't directly related to the garden. So no tea and biscuits.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "389f744e8eed7e775d74d4a446ee4c8e4879914cbc035cb4a6ef84d33fb995de",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "david",
        "speaker": "David",
        "sourceStart": 324,
        "sourceEnd": 492,
        "text": "Option A is a new shed for storing tools. The old one is falling apart, and tools are getting rusty. A replacement would cost 400 pounds, leaving 100 for small repairs.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "f097485e51d71f597e243370dae8a07ebf5e613c17464f514821281da01317ab",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "anna",
        "speaker": "Anna",
        "sourceStart": 499,
        "sourceEnd": 658,
        "text": "Option B is a water butt system to collect rainwater. That would cost around 300 pounds and should reduce our water bills. It also supports water conservation.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "52f689ffa6a12872b812805a687a6d215ab94cf20b3a960104f7f938f96001f0",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "david",
        "speaker": "David",
        "sourceStart": 666,
        "sourceEnd": 775,
        "text": "Option C is a seating area. Standard benches would cost 350 pounds and might attract visitors and volunteers.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "2d0a9605692380c79fff5b29e7b728f1d2cc79f6a269acab62940380449f2a04",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "anna",
        "speaker": "Anna",
        "sourceStart": 782,
        "sourceEnd": 954,
        "text": "We should consider the survey from last month. 60 percent said they wanted better facilities for sitting, 20 percent wanted storage, and the rest wanted water conservation.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "59dfd3a0514ac5433a14a9dd4df8472e01ac6157c31d7f5b9ffbb21b18f34667",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "david",
        "speaker": "David",
        "sourceStart": 962,
        "sourceEnd": 1093,
        "text": "Oh, I didn't know about that survey. That changes things. Seating is the most popular, although we need to consider durability too.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "88f7fe0dfe57b3f3dd1821fbef25b00ae6a4905b5d73583d5520d528d92b1542",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "anna",
        "speaker": "Anna",
        "sourceStart": 1100,
        "sourceEnd": 1251,
        "text": "You're right. One correction: 350 pounds is for standard benches. Weatherproof ones would be 450 pounds. They cost more but should last longer outside.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "99c1653eab833b8ff636599870d9770ed042410a83abbb712e370ccb5a8e267b",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "david",
        "speaker": "David",
        "sourceStart": 1259,
        "sourceEnd": 1452,
        "text": "If we choose weatherproof benches, we can't afford the water butt as well. A compromise would be to buy the water butt for 300 pounds and use the remaining 200 pounds for a simple bench or two.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "a2ac330704f68ee7a46805c905b19c1897a2e90b905211055436975e5e8ac621",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "anna",
        "speaker": "Anna",
        "sourceStart": 1459,
        "sourceEnd": 1577,
        "text": "That's a compromise, but it leaves the storage problem. We could ask for shed donations, though nothing is guaranteed.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "6d482e5c7a28f22d72117dd767c96a1aa3488685cbc3b0e9f75370567f82b9bd",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "david",
        "speaker": "David",
        "sourceStart": 1585,
        "sourceEnd": 1776,
        "text": "We have to prioritize. The shed solves storage but is less popular according to the survey. The water butt saves water but doesn't provide seating. Weatherproof seating is popular but costly.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "4adb834992854fad70f3b34e00f1d2178aefb4ab49ac57705282be097b97f258",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "anna",
        "speaker": "Anna",
        "sourceStart": 1783,
        "sourceEnd": 1978,
        "text": "We also need to consider maintenance costs. A shed might need repairs; the water butt needs little maintenance; standard wooden benches might need varnishing. Purchase price isn't the whole cost.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "4eae725d74630ac2982cf198a8ac2d8ceb34356b0f2260bddef642d5f1306c92",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "david",
        "speaker": "David",
        "sourceStart": 1986,
        "sourceEnd": 2129,
        "text": "Let's vote on the three main options before discussing any combination further: A, shed; B, water butt; C, seating area. Raise your hand for A.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "7d3ebb784ff5dd970bc97c70c6a540d113df906f7bbb0c01919074fb9dfa1172",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      }
    ]
  },
